'))\nend)\n\ntest('helmprov: PATH_AT names the values key under the cursor; CHART_OF finds the chart; USE_ITEMS are quickfix rows', function ()\n    ready()\n    local root = chart(CHART)\n    local buf = vim.fn.bufadd(root .. '/values.yaml'); vim.fn.bufload(buf)\n    eq('image.tag', P.path_at(buf, 2, 3))\n    eq('port', P.path_at(buf, 3, 0))\n    eq(vim.fn.fnamemodify(root, ':p'):gsub('/$', ''), P.chart_of(root .. '/templates/deployment.yaml'))\n    local items, src = P.use_items(root, 'image.tag')\n    eq('rendered', src)\n    eq(2, #items); eq(2, items[1].lnum); ok(items[1].filename:match('_helpers%.tpl$')); eq(16, items[2].lnum)\n    vim.api.nvim_buf_delete(buf, { force = true })\nend)\n\ntest('helmprov: without a render the use sites fall back to the STATIC reads, said so', function ()\n    if not pcall(vim.treesitter.get_string_parser, '', 'yaml') then skip 'no yaml parser' end\n    local root = chart(CHART)\n    local render = P.render\n    P.render = function () return nil, 'stubbed' end\n    local okc, items, src = pcall(P.use_items, root, 'port')\n    P.render = render\n    ok(okc, tostring(items))\n    eq('static', src)\n    eq(1, #items); eq(12, items[1].lnum)\nend)\n"},"verb":"edit"},"bytes":142,"decided_by":"tactic","verb":"edit","decisions":[],"id":"1790898177.699880-edit"},{"invocation":{"touched":[".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"],"args":{"after":"| Which Helm templates are WRONG while every tool reports success — a values typo that renders empty, a values key nothing reads, a record separator the chomp deletes, a checksum annotation that does not roll the pod? | `local L = require 'cartograph.helmlint'; local r = L.lint(<chart dir>, { render = true|false }); print(table.concat(L.lines(r), '\\n'))` — templates read with the `helm` tree-sitter grammar: `dangling-values-path` (`.Values.a.b` read, values.yaml never defines it; a read guarded by `if`/`with` on that path, piped to or an ARGUMENT of `default` / `required` / `coalesce` is not one; \"defined up to\" names the prefix), `orphan-value` (a defined leaf no read covers; subchart keys and `global` excluded; REFUSED when a template reads `.Values` whole or via `index`), `chomped-separator` (a `range` inside a YAML block scalar `key: |` whose closing `{{- end` chomps the blank line between records — LDIF/PEM; the license-header chomp idiom is not one), `checksum-under-coverage` (needs the render: a `checksum/…` pod annotation's hashed values / included files against the values read by the template that produces each ConfigMap / Secret the pod references). Frontiers said: a library chart (its helpers read the includer's values), `.Values` relative to a rebound dot in range/with, and static values as a hypothetical release (`helm upgrade` reuses the last values). Measured: microservices-demo 1 finding (orphan `googleCloudOperations.metrics`, verified), helm's testcharts 2 dangling (both deliberate fixtures) after the library rule. MCP: `helm_chart` (rows), `k8s_findings` (the post-pass on this graph), `helm_stages` (stages and drift of the graph root). CART-0156 |\n| Where is a Helm VALUE used — from the `values.yaml` key under my cursor to every template line that reads it, helpers included — and which template line WROTE a given rendered byte or field? | `:CartographHelmUses` on a values key (the key path from the YAML tree: `images.tag` on `tag:` under `images:`) fills the quickfix with every read; `:CartographHelmLint` lints the chart of the buffer. In Lua: `local P = require 'cartograph.helmprov'; local p = P.render(<chart>, { release, namespace, values = { f }, set = { 'k=v' } })` — HELM'S OWN ENGINE over a copy of text/template that keeps what the executor knows (tools/helmprov, built OFFLINE on first use against the local helm checkout and the Go module cache): `p.files[<chart>/templates/x.yaml]` = { content, spans = { { start, end, loc = 'file:line:col', kind } } } (every rendered byte range → the template node that wrote it; a text span reproduces its source byte for byte; an action's loc is its pipeline, just inside `{{`), `p.reads` = { { path, loc } } (every evaluated `.Values` chain, at the node that evaluated it — inside an included helper, not on the include line). `P.uses(p, 'a.b')` (reads of it, a descendant, or an ancestor: `toYaml .Values.a` uses a.b), `P.position(p, file, byte)` (exact template file/line/col), `P.locate(p, kind, name, text)` (a rendered document's text → its template position), `P.path_at(buf, row, col)`, `P.use_items(chart, path)` (quickfix rows; falls back to helmlint's STATIC reads when it does not build, said `static`). Frontiers: bytes an `include` writes are attributed to the include action (the helper's reads are not lost); `.Values` relative to a dot rebound by range/with is not a read; only the branches this values set takes are seen (CART-0871 is all branches). Measured on microservices-demo: 13/13 rendered files equal `helm template`'s documents, 530/530 text spans reproduce their source, 327 reads; `images.tag` → 11 sites. CART-0870 |\n","file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md","before":"| Which Helm templates are WRONG while every tool reports success — a values typo that renders empty, a values key nothing reads, a record separator the chomp deletes, a checksum annotation that does not roll the pod? | `local L = require 'cartograph.helmlint'; local r = L.lint(<chart dir>, { render = true|false }); print(table.concat(L.lines(r), '\\n'))` — templates read with the `helm` tree-sitter grammar: `dangling-values-path` (`.Values.a.b` read, values.yaml never defines it; a read guarded by `if`/`with` on that path, piped to or an ARGUMENT of `default` / `required` / `coalesce` is not one; \"defined up to\" names the prefix), `orphan-value` (a defined leaf no read covers; subchart keys and `global` excluded; REFUSED when a template reads `.Values` whole or via `index`), `chomped-separator` (a `range` inside a YAML block scalar `key: |` whose closing `{{- end` chomps the blank line between records — LDIF/PEM; the license-header chomp idiom is not one), `checksum-under-coverage` (needs the render: a `checksum/…` pod annotation's hashed values / included files against the values read by the template that produces each ConfigMap / Secret the pod references). Frontiers said: a library chart (its helpers read the includer's values), `.Values` relative to a rebound dot in range/with, and static values as a hypothetical release (`helm upgrade` reuses the last values). Measured: microservices-demo 1 finding (orphan `googleCloudOperations.metrics`, verified), helm's testcharts 2 dangling (both deliberate fixtures) after the library rule. MCP: `helm_chart` (rows), `k8s_findings` (the post-pass on this graph), `helm_stages` (stages and drift of the graph root). CART-0156 |\n"},"verb":"edit"},"bytes":1970,"decided_by":"tactic","verb":"edit","decisions":[],"id":"1790898232.394018-edit"}],"hand":0,"open_intents":[],"commit":"e819b558af4d32e423fef897a6aed14d517933c0","version":1}
